Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and is not covered by a tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs planning permission unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So:

- If you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the pattern (for example, the glazing bar layout or opening style), you will likely need to submit a planning application before starting.
- If the replacements are an exact match in both material and pattern, you may not need an application. Because this is a judgement call, please check with the planning desk before you order or start work.

I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal. If you have a planning reference for any earlier work at the property, I can look up its status and history.
